@startuml
title TraceLeft Architecture - Component View

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

rectangle "Userspace" {
  [TraceLeft CLI] as CLI
  [Trace Command] as TraceCmd
  [Event Registration Parser] as RegParser
  [TraceLeft Library] as Lib
  [Probe Loader] as Loader
  [Userspace Tracer/Dispatcher] as Tracer
  [Generator Subsystem] as Generator
  database "Event Config Metadata\n(Proto/JSON)" as EventConfig
  artifact "Generated eBPF\nHandler Source Code" as GeneratedHandlers
  [gobpf Integration] as Gobpf
}

node "Linux Kernel (eBPF)" as Kernel {
  [Main eBPF Program] as MainProg
  collections "Handler Maps\nhandle_NAME_progs\nhandle_NAME_progs_ret" as HandlerMaps
  folder "kprobe/kretprobe Hooks" as Hooks
  [Handler eBPF Programs\n(default + process-specific)] as Handlers
  queue "Perf Event Channel" as Perf
  [Common Event Header] as CommonHeader
}

CLI --> TraceCmd : invoke trace
TraceCmd --> RegParser : parse args
RegParser --> Loader : event registration {ProgramID,Pids,ELFPath}
Loader --> Gobpf : load probes/handlers
Gobpf --> MainProg : load & attach
MainProg --> Hooks : attach
MainProg --> HandlerMaps : select by process context
MainProg --> Handlers : tail call/select handler
Handlers --> Perf : emit events
Perf --> Tracer : deliver events
Tracer --> Lib : dispatch using header
EventConfig --> Generator : read metadata
Generator --> GeneratedHandlers : generate sources
GeneratedHandlers --> Loader : compile/build & load handlers

note right of RegParser
Produces event registration structure:
- ProgramID
- Pids
- ELFPath
end note

note right of Loader
Loads default and process-specific handler probes.
Recognizes naming scheme for maps and probes.
end note

note right of HandlerMaps
Map naming:
- handle_NAME_progs
- handle_NAME_progs_ret
Probe naming:
- kprobe/handle_NAME
- kretprobe/handle_NAME
NAME identifies the traced function.
end note

note right of Handlers
If no handler is configured for a probe,
the probe performs no handler action and returns 0.
end note

note bottom of Perf
Perf-based channel transferring events from kernel to userspace.
end note

note right of CommonHeader
All emitted events begin with this common leading section,
enabling userspace dispatch.
end note

note bottom of Kernel
Requires Linux with eBPF, kprobe, and kretprobe support.
end note

note bottom of Gobpf
Technology constraint: implementation integrates via gobpf.
end note

@enduml